# PTT (Phan-Thien–Tanner) 3D planar-extension canary for the KRK-VE-3D
# dispatch. The production driver (run_viscoelastic_fvfd_extensional_3d) imposes
# the planar-extension velocity field u = (epsilon_dot*x, -epsilon_dot*y, 0) on
# a coarse box and advances psi = log(C) to the fixed point. No obstacle or
# inflow/outflow geometry is needed: velocity_mode=:imposed.
#
# The PTT closure multiplies the relaxation by the scalar trace multiplier
#   Y(trC) = 1 + epsilon·(trC − 3)        (linear variant, variant = 0)
# enhancing relaxation of stretched modes. At lambda = 50 and
# epsilon_dot = 0.005 (lambda*epsilon_dot = 0.25), Oldroyd-B would reach
# C_xx = 1/(1 − 2*lambda*epsilon_dot) = 2.0; the trace multiplier reduces this
# stretch (C_xx < 2). As epsilon → 0 the result recovers the Oldroyd-B
# planar-extension fixed point bit-identically. The variant is numeric:
# 0 = linear (default), 1 = exponential (Y = exp(epsilon·(trC − 3))).
# beta = nu_s/(nu_s+nu_p) = 0.5 with nu_total = 0.1.
Simulation extensional_ptt D3Q19

Define epsilon_dot = 0.005

Domain L = 24 x 24 x 6  N = 24 x 24 x 6
Physics epsilon_dot = epsilon_dot
Rheology ptt { nu_s = 0.05 nu_p = 0.05 lambda = 50 epsilon = 0.2 variant = 0 }
Module viscoelastic

Run 1000 steps
